<title>FRANCE: Pinault-Printemps H1 profit rises.</title>
<headline>Pinault-Printemps H1 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     748  vs	     452</p>
<p>    Operating				    1,295  vs	   1,084</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional		 1,134  vs	     803</p>
<p>    Exceptional			  charges  64  vs   charges 207</p>
<p>    Financial expense			    161  vs	     281</p>
<p>    Turnover				    37,745  vs	  37,187</p>
<p>NOTE - Pinault-Printemps-Redoute issued its results in a statement. It said cashflow in the first half of 1996 rose 32.7 percent to 1.37 billion francs.</p>
<p>Operational investments were 492 million francs in the first half.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
